AB  - This article has been retracted: please see Elsevier's Policy on Article Withdrawal (https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/article-withdrawal). This article has been retracted at the request of the Editor. Following publication, concerns were raised regarding the scientific reliability and integrity of the article. These included potential scientific misconduct, such as plagiarism, suspected paper mill activity, the possible use of AI-generated or manipulated figures, and errors in data presentation. During the journal's assessment, substantial issues were identified with the presentation and interpretation of figures. The purpose and scientific significance of the zone map presented in Fig. 1 could not be clearly established. Fig. 3 does not adequately characterise temporal or spatial variability as claimed, and the legend of Fig. 9 obscures the underlying graphical content, preventing meaningful interpretation. Additional figures were also found to contain graphical and presentation deficiencies that undermine their scientific value. Concerns were further raised regarding the reference list. We identified fourteen citations that benefitted an individual and which were irrelevant to the article. Several other references were likewise found to be irrelevant to the study's stated aims. Taking into account the cumulative seriousness of these issues and their impact on the reliability of the findings, the Editor-in-Chief has decided to retract the article to maintain the integrity of the scientific record. The authors have been informed of this retraction. The journal apologizes to its readers that these issues were not identified prior to publication. © 2026 The Author(s).
