TI  - A novel context-aware retrieval framework for biomedical knowledge integration with large language models
AU  - Kumari, M.
AU  - Chauhan, R.
AU  - Jain, R.
AU  - Garg, P.
T2  - Information Fusion
AB  - The integration of large language models (LLMs) into biomedical domains faces critical challenges including knowledge retrieval limitations and hallucinations. This study presents BiomedKAI, a novel multi-agent architecture integrating dynamically updated biomedical knowledge graphs with pre-trained LLMs as a scalable alternative to domain-specific model training. The framework introduces CARE-RAG (Context-Aware Retrieval-Enhanced Generation), which implements query-type-aware retrieval strategies that dynamically adjust search parameters, traversal depths, and scoring weights based on classified query intent. CARE-RAG addresses limitations in traditional RAG systems by combining vector semantic search with depth-governed graph exploration and relevance-weighted entity prioritization to minimize information loss. Six specialized agents (Diagnostic, Treatment, Drug Interaction, General Medical, Preventive Care, and Research) operate on a comprehensive biomedical knowledge graph containing 43,000 genes, 230,000 proteins, 17,380 drugs, and 12,119 diseases. Experimental validation demonstrates: 84.4% accuracy on MedQA examinations, 85.7% diagnostic precision on NEJM clinical cases (versus 64% for GPT-4), and 99.22% effectiveness in identifying medical misinformation, while achieving 66.5% token efficiency compared to conventional RAG. These results indicate CARE-RAG enables general-purpose LLMs to achieve expert-level biomedical performance with computational efficiency. The tool is freely available at:  http://pitools.niper.ac.in/BiomedKAI/home . © 2025 Elsevier B.V.
