TI  - Improved Uni-Modal Chinese Fake News Detection Leveraging User Comments
AU  - Zhang, L.
AU  - Zhao, X.
T2  - 2025 6th International Conference on Computer Vision and Data Mining, ICCVDM 2025
AB  - Relying solely on the textual content of news pieces is often insufficient for effective fake news detection (FND), as misleading information is frequently crafted with the intent to deceive readers. However, related discussions on social media platforms such as Weibo and X (formerly Twitter) often provide valuable context through user comments. These responses can serve as a critical signal in evaluating the authenticity of news. In this paper, we demonstrate that incorporating user comments into a uni-modal FND pipeline significantly enhances its performance. Specifically, we leverage the [CLS] token representation obtained from a BERT-based encoder for the target news piece and combine it with the vector representations of associated user comments using a Transformer-Based fusion module. This simple yet effective integration sets a new state-of-the-art on the largest Chinese FND dataset, Weibo-21, improving the previous best macro F1-score from 0.943 (BERT-EMO) to 0.97748. Code is at https://github.com/lezhang-thu/Chinese-Fnd-weibo21 to facilitate further research. © 2025 IEEE.
