AU  - Das, S.
AU  - Karmakar, S.
AU  - Das, T.
T2  - Effects of Education Communication in Digital Learning Environments
AB  - In the digital era, misinformation or false information shared without intent to deceive significantly impacts education by undermining student engagement, learning outcomes, and critical thinking. Misinformation arises from misunderstandings or unverified sources and spreads rapidly through digital platforms, influencing perceptions and creating challenges for educators. This study highlights key objectives, including examining misinformation's impact, identifying challenges for educators, and exploring strategies to address these issues. Findings emphasize the need for critical digital literacy and media literacy integration into curricula. Strategies to overcome these challenges include professional development for educators, leveraging fact- checking tools, and fostering open dialogue to build students' critical evaluation skills. The study calls for institutional support and collaborative efforts to create a resilient educational framework that counters misinformation and enhances the effectiveness of digital learning. © 2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
