TI  - An artificial intelligence (AI)-based cyber security system for managing financial sector
AU  - Revathy, S.
AU  - Valliammal, M.
AU  - Manivannan, S.K.
AU  - Sha, S.N.
T2  - AIP Conference Proceedings
AB  - Cyber threats include deliberate efforts to improve unauthorized access to, manipulate, or erase confidential details, extort cash from casualties, or disrupt corporate operations. Traditional network security approaches need more scalability, slow reaction times, and a lack of ability to detect attacks. These imperfections emphasize the need for research to develop more efficient protection techniques against increasing network threats. Cybercriminals use Artificial Intelligence (AI), data poisoning techniques, and model stealing schemes to automate their assaults. This research introduces a Cyber Security (CS) approach that utilizes AI to manage the banking industry. AI is a very effective technology for mapping and mitigating unforeseen hazards that might threaten a corporation. The K-Nearest Neighbor (KNN) method generates forecasts by acquiring knowledge from the training information. Within finance, it serves the purpose of identifying and preventing malware assaults. The suggested strategy enhances the efficacy of cyber security mechanisms by bolstering their resilience against assaults. The system demonstrates analytical scores of 52.87% for data privacy, 86.02% for scalability, and 82.09% for data protection ratio. © 2026 Author(s).
