AB  - This article has been retracted: please see Elsevier policy on Article Correction, Retraction and Removal (https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies-and-standards/article-withdrawal). This article has been retracted at the request of the Editor-in-Chief following the outcome of an investigation conducted by Auburn University into the work of the corresponding author. The investigation identified acts of fabrication, falsification, and/or plagiarism involving Figs. 1, 4(b), 4(c), 11, 12(a), 12(b), 12(c), 12(d), and 12(e) of the published article. Specifically, these figures were found to be misappropriated or manipulated from the following published sources: • Curr Opin Solid State Mater Sci. 2022 Jan;26(2):1–124. doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cossms.2021.100974 • Int. J. Fatigue. 2017 May;98:14–31. doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijfatigue.2017.01.001 • Mater. Sci. Eng. A. 2016 Feb;655:100–112. doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.msea.2015.12.026 • Sci Rep. 2021 Oct;11:20424. doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-99,959-6 • Mater. Sci. Eng. A. 2021 May;814:141194. doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.msea.2021.141194 • Acta Materialia. 2010 May;58(9):3303–3312. doi: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actamat.2010.02.004 Auburn University determined by a preponderance of evidence that the fabrication, falsification, and/or plagiarism were committed intentionally by the corresponding author. These actions represent a significant departure from accepted research practices and ethical standards. Importantly, the investigation found no evidence indicating that any of the co-authors were involved in or aware of the misconduct described above. The Editor-in-Chief considers this a serious breach of publication ethics and has therefore retracted the article. © 2023
