TI  - Polarforming for Wireless Networks: Opportunities and Challenges
AU  - Ding, J.
AU  - Zhou, Z.
AU  - Shao, X.
AU  - Jiao, B.
AU  - Zhang, R.
T2  - IEEE Communications Magazine
AB  - Polarforming emerges as a promising technique for manipulating the polarization of electromagnetic (EM) waves by shaping the polarization of an antenna into a desired state. By dynamically adjusting antenna polarization, polarforming enables real-time polarization matching or mis-matching with received EM waves, thereby leveraging polarization degrees of freedom (DoFs) to enhance wireless communication performance. In this article, we first present an overview of the fundamental principles and design approaches underlying the polarforming technique. Then, we analyze the key advantages of polarforming, including hardware cost reduction, depolarization mitigation, channel adaptation, and signal quality improvement. Furthermore, we explore promising applications of polarforming for next-generation wireless networks. Finally, we discuss the implementation challenges and their potential solutions, motivating future research.  © 2026 IEEE.
