TY  - CONF
TI  - Enhancing Productivity in Educational Institutions with an AI-Powered Real-Time Schedule Management System
AU  - Rajamoorthy, R.
AU  - Karthik, S.
AU  - Savitha, S.
AU  - Sindhu, M.
AU  - Devi, S.V.
AU  - Vihitha, V.
T2  - Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems
AB  - The Real-time Schedule Management Project is an innovation aimed at improving scheduling within educational facilities. With the support from leading-edge technology, including AI voice-to-text features, students and authorities are able to make scheduling more efficient and effective. The project has been designed to address failures of standard scheduling practices, which include failure in communication, scheduling delays, and updates that are quite a task to handle single-handedly. The main feature of this system is that it has the feature of AI-enabled voice recognition, which allows inputting scheduling data by the authorities using their voice. It will also eliminate the tedium of writing and misplacing, hence going for a more efficient and quicker way of handling the schedules. The system also handles appointments automatically; hence, students are availed with real-time information on the availability of higher authorities, saving on appointment time wastage. This feature improves general time management for the students and improves their ability to schedule without incidence of overlapping conversations or appointments. The project technically has put together a strong combination of both the front end and the back end. The front end is created using XML in order to be flexible and structure the user interface so it can showcase a clean and responsive design. SQLite is a lightweight database system preinstalled in the backend of the mobile application for local data storage. Moreover, data in the application may be stored securely in 000webhost, as it is a cloud system that can hold data efficiently and consistently. For communication between the frontend and backend, there is access to the API through Volley, which further integrates toward ensuring a smooth exchange of information between the two ends. Combining these technologies certainly enables an unbroken flow of data and leads toward the expected quality of service. The system was designed with security at the forefront. Using access control, the authorities are given secure login details in order to protect their schedules. Such measures ensure that confidential data remains safe and allow people to have access to change it. With the students using the system, they are provided with simple means of watching marks without any chance of manipulating the data available in the interface of the system. Scalability is, of course, one of the greatest advantages of a project. Even though it is mostly focused on representing educational establishments, the architecture of the system and its functionalities can be modified for other areas like corporate offices, hospitals, or any other organization needing an effective system of scheduling. It's important to outline that voice recognition driven by artificial intelligence is one of the most distinguishable features that put this solution in front of the rest. With regards to the project's goals, user convenience is also a factor put in consideration alongside its technical features. The interaction of the system is impeccable, as both the students and authorities could get information in real time. This reduces the training required for users and aids in increasing usage breadth. The system reduces such scheduling work and leaves higher work for the other authorities and hence raises the output overall. The Real-time Schedule Management Project is a safe and efficient project that eliminates problems relating to the old booking systems. Their development in AI and technology, at the base, makes this even more sophisticated for educational institutes, though it can be more useful for other spheres too. This project is one of the major strides toward taking a more progressive approach geared toward schedule management and a better experience for users across various environments. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2026.
