TY  - JOUR
TI  - Study on the influence path of data asset information disclosure level and its high-quality development effect in large innovative enterprises
AU  - Xinzhong, B.
AU  - Jiahang, L.
T2  - Technology Analysis and Strategic Management
AB  - We adopt the fsQCA and double machine learning methods to explore the influencing paths of the data asset information disclosure level of large innovative enterprises and their corresponding high-quality development effects. We find that: (1) Data asset information disclosure levels of large innovative enterprises are driven by the interplay of disclosure motivation, opportunity, and ability; (2) Five configurational paths drive the high-level data asset information disclosure in large innovative enterprises, namely ‘Opportunity-Seizing under Market Pressure’, ‘Capability Support under Media Attention’, ‘Independent Director-Driven under Analyst Attention’, ‘Capability Guarantee’, and ‘Comprehensive Linkage’; four paths drive non-high-level disclosure, collectively named ‘Executive Capability Constraint under Strong Supervision by Independent Directors’; (3) Only large innovative enterprises with genuine high-level data assets can promote their high-quality development by improving the information environment and optimising labour structure, those manipulating data asset information disclosure through ‘symbolic than substantive’ cannot achieve this goal. © 2026 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
