TY  - JOUR
TI  - Study on the Mode of User Algorithmic Choosing Based on Privacy Calculus
AU  - Hou, Z.
AU  - Yihan, X.
T2  - Journal of Modern Information
AB  - [Purpose/Significance]Algorithms are widely applied in smart media,bringing convenience to users in accessing information,but also causing severe issues of collective privacy leakage. Users may enjoy the convenience brought by algorithms,but they might also resist algorithms through avoidance,noise addition,and other methods. This paper analyzes the optimal strategy for users’algorithm choices and their behavior patterns from the perspective of privacy calculus. This study overcomes the issues of algorithm invisibility and measurement challenges by proposing a measurement framework for users′ algorithm selection behavior. The findings provide a theoretical foundation for product design and regulation in relevant fields.[Method/Process]Using user personal information and behavior trajectory data from the Zhihu platform,user privacy orientation and algorithm choice strategies were analyzed through item response theory and word vector methods,exploring the algorithm choice patterns of users with different privacy orientation.[Result/Conclusion]Empirical results indicate that,when interacting with algorithms,protection-oriented users exhibits stronger algorithm resistance behaviors. Meanwhile,disclosure-oriented users are unlikely to manipulate the algorithm. © 2026 Editorial Board of Journal of Modern Information. All rights reserved.
