AB  - In the digital age, images play a pivotal role in both criminal investigations and national security efforts. Using these cutting-edge techniques and technologies to authenticate, analyze, and interpret digital images for forensic purposes help with national security efforts. With the rise of sophisticated image manipulation and deepfakes, law enforcement and security professionals face growing challenges in distinguishing real evidence from fabricated content. Using these modern tools and methodologies are transforming digital forensics and strengthening the integrity of investigative processes. Advancements in Forensic Analysis of Digital Images for Security and Law Enforcement delves into cutting-edge technologies for image authentication, biometric watermarking and the integration of computer vision in criminal investigations. It highlights real-world applications in areas including digital evidence validation, crime scene reconstruction, and surveillance enhancement. Covering topics such as blockchain, forensics, and surveillance footage, this book is an excellent resource for designers and engineers, law enforcement and security professionals, educators, postgraduate students, researchers, academicians, and more. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing.
