AB  - The advent of social media has significantly contributed to the dissemination of information during health emergencies, particularly during the outbreak of mpox. Employing the theory of planned behavior (TPB;), the current study evaluated how social factors predicted mpox vaccination intention. Surveying college students, the study found that individuals who were more likely to believe misinformation about mpox were less likely to hold intentions to receive the mpox vaccine and that individuals with higher levels of concern about mpox were more likely to hold intentions of receiving the mpox vaccine. In addition, those who identified as more conservative in their political views were less likely to hold mpox vaccination intentions. Future research can apply the findings of this study as a framework for examining future pandemics, epidemics, and health crises. © 2025 Southern States Communication Association.
